Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||04-19-2001||01:50 AM||||think a shop might be rippin me, how do i tell if the heads i got with a longblock are fiero ones? this is kinda urgent because my return option ends tomorrow||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||04-19-2001||02:19 AM||||I always thought the only difference was the valve size.  GM just put bigger valves in the standard output castings.<P> intakes:  1.72 vs 1.6<BR>exhausts:  1.42 vs 1.3<P>But I bet you're looking for a number cast into the head somewhere.||||reg||12
Z||000002||Steven||04-19-2001||01:31 PM||||The heads that came on 2.8 Fiero were 14054884. You should be able to find that number on top of the heads. GM also had an older number on the heads. It was a 14054879, and that came with the correct (larger) valves. As a matter of fact the 14054879 is now dicontinued and replaced by the 14054884. Look for either of those numbers.<P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
